\item The argument spelling that the real \code{sinfo} and \code{squeue} accept.
\item The output grammar that the real \code{sinfo} and \code{squeue} produce.
\item Which users' jobs \code{squeue} reports. The check reads every job the caller
can see, and no option scopes it to one user.
\item That two \code{submit.sh} runs started at the same time cannot both pass.
